{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++0x code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++0x code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <limits>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing int64 = long long;\n\nint64 gcd(int64 a, int64 b) {\n    for (; b != 0; ) {\n        a %= b;\n        swap(a, b);\n    }\n    return a;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int64 x, y, n;\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n\n    int64 best_num = 0, best_den = 1;\n    double smallest_error = numeric_limits<double>::max();\n\n    for (int64 denom = 1; denom <= n; ++denom) {\n        int64 num_floor = 0;\n        int64 left = 0, right = 100000;\n        while (left <= right) {\n            int64 mid = (left + right) >> 1;\n            if (mid * y <= x * denom) {\n                num_floor = mid;\n                left = mid + 1;\n            } else {\n                right = mid - 1;\n            }\n        }\n\n        int64 num_ceil = 0;\n        left = 0, right = 100000;\n        while (left <= right) {\n            int64 mid = (left + right) >> 1;\n            if (mid * y < x * denom) {\n                left = mid + 1;\n            } else {\n                num_ceil = mid;\n                right = mid - 1;\n            }\n        }\n\n        double err_floor = fabs(static_cast<double>(num_floor) / denom - static_cast<double>(x) / y);\n        double err_ceil = fabs(static_cast<double>(num_ceil) / denom - static_cast<double>(x) / y);\n\n        int64 chosen_num = num_floor;\n        int64 chosen_den = denom;\n        double chosen_err = err_floor;\n\n        if (err_ceil < err_floor - 1e-9) {\n            chosen_num = num_ceil;\n            chosen_den = denom;\n            chosen_err = err_ceil;\n        }\n\n        int64 g = gcd(chosen_num, chosen_den);\n        chosen_num /= g;\n        chosen_den /= g;\n\n        if (chosen_err < smallest_error) {\n            best_num = chosen_num;\n            best_den = chosen_den;\n            smallest_error = chosen_err;\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << best_num << \"/\" << best_den << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static long gcd(long a, long b) {\n        while (b != 0) {\n            long temp = a % b;\n            a = b;\n            b = temp;\n        }\n        return a;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long x = scanner.nextLong();\n        long y = scanner.nextLong();\n        long n = scanner.nextLong();\n\n        long best_num = 0;\n        long best_den = 1;\n        double smallest_error = Double.MAX_VALUE;\n\n        for (long denom = 1; denom <= n; ++denom) {\n            long num_floor = 0;\n            long left = 0, right = 100000;\n            while (left <= right) {\n                long mid = (left + right) >> 1;\n                if (mid * y <= x * denom) {\n                    num_floor = mid;\n                    left = mid + 1;\n                } else {\n                    right = mid - 1;\n                }\n            }\n\n            long num_ceil = 0;\n            left = 0;\n            right = 100000;\n            while (left <= right) {\n                long mid = (left + right) >> 1;\n                if (mid * y < x * denom) {\n                    left = mid + 1;\n                } else {\n                    num_ceil = mid;\n                    right = mid - 1;\n                }\n            }\n\n            double err_floor = Math.abs((double) num_floor / denom - (double) x / y);\n            double err_ceil = Math.abs((double) num_ceil / denom - (double) x / y);\n\n            long chosen_num = num_floor;\n            long chosen_den = denom;\n            double chosen_err = err_floor;\n\n            if (err_ceil < err_floor - 1e-9) {\n                chosen_num = num_ceil;\n                chosen_den = denom;\n                chosen_err = err_ceil;\n            }\n\n            long g = gcd(chosen_num, chosen_den);\n            chosen_num /= g;\n            chosen_den /= g;\n\n            if (chosen_err < smallest_error) {\n                best_num = chosen_num;\n                best_den = chosen_den;\n                smallest_error = chosen_err;\n            }\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(best_num + \"/\" + best_den);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00012933371181134135, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -7.486063259420916e-05, -8.34461570775602e-06, -0.004513077903538942, -0.46069371700286865, -1.156323378381785e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.351044481154531e-05, -0.000710592488758266, -0.00012385078298393637, -0.04531555250287056, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -0.06243810057640076, -1.5616295058862306e-05, -4.076874756719917e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -3.325883881188929e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, -9.179073458653875e-06, -0.04859539121389389, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -2.384185